# This directory is for Docker image tarballs transferred from connected environments
# 
# The GitLab CI pipeline expects Docker image tarballs at:
#   /transfer/spel-builder-*.tar.gz (or .tar.gz.b64 if using SharePoint)
#
# To prepare the tarball:
#   1. Run the offline-prepare.yml workflow in GitHub Actions
#   2. Download the spel-builder-YYYYMMDD artifact
#   3. Choose the appropriate format for your transfer method:
#
# BINARY FORMAT (recommended for most transfers):
#   - File: spel-builder-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz (~305 MB)
#   - Use for: Direct downloads, USB drives, DVDs, SCP, SFTP
#   - Transfer to: this directory
#
# BASE64 FORMAT (required for SharePoint):
#   - File: spel-builder-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz.b64 (~407 MB)
#   - Use for: SharePoint transfers (avoids binary corruption)
#   - Transfer to: this directory
#   - Note: GitLab CI automatically decodes .b64 files before import
#
# Optional: Include checksum file for verification:
#   sha256sum spel-builder-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz > spel-builder-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz.sha256
